            "status": "active",
            "contribution_type": "adjustment",
            "exact_contribution": {
                "added": [
                    "Parenting expert Denise Stern says to burp after every ounce of bottled milk or when switching breasts, and again when feeding ends. Place the baby over your shoulder or on your lap with the head supported and rub or pat their back until they burp. Hold them upright for 10-15 minutes before putting them down to sleep."
                ],
                "removed": [
                    "Baby care expert Denise Stern says to burp a bottle-fed baby after each ounce of milk, or a breastfed baby when switching breasts. Burp again when feeding ends. Place the baby over your shoulder or on your lap with the head supported. Hold them upright for 10-15 minutes before putting them down to sleep after feeding."
                ]
            }
        },
        {
            "id": "33535025",
            "user": "Seymour Edits",
            "timestamp": "22:35, 6 July 2025",
            "anon": false,
            "size": "(8,555 bytes)",
