            "status": "active",
            "contribution_type": "addition",
            "exact_contribution": {
                "added": [
                    "{{ParagraphTYSK}}Burping helps babies release air that becomes trapped in their stomach. Burping is often most effective right after or in between a feeding, when a baby sucks in extra air while feeding on milk or food. Burping your baby will help him or her release that air, improving their feeding and general comfort. Burping is quite easy if you know what to do.",
                    "[[Category:Baby Health]]",
                    "==The Best Ways to Burp a Baby==",
                    "Baby care expert Denise Stern says to burp a bottle-fed baby after each ounce of milk, or a breastfed baby when switching breasts. Burp again when feeding ends. Place the baby over your shoulder or on your lap with the head supported. Hold them upright for 10-15 minutes before putting them down to sleep after feeding."
                ],
                "removed": [
                    "Burping helps babies release air that becomes trapped in their stomach. Burping is often most effective right after or in between a feeding, when a baby sucks in extra air while feeding on milk or food. Burping your baby will help him or her release that air, improving their feeding and general comfort. Burping is quite easy if you know what to do.",
                    "[[Category:Baby Health]]"
                ]
            }
        },
