                    "",
                    "==Quick Overview==",
                    "Before burping your baby, hold them over your shoulder and put a burping cloth on your shoulder. Then, you want to pat them gently between the shoulder blades or rub their back using a circular motion. Always listen for the baby burping, and stop patting their back when you hear them doing so. Now, put them in front of you, show them your pleased by smiling at your baby, and give them a kiss to let them know you’re there. Finally, you can try frequent but light breastfeeding sessions instead of bottle feeding to reduce the need to burp your baby."
                ]
            }
        },
